# aetelier-sdk/serve/aetelier-validate.cron
#
# Drop this file into /etc/cron.d/aetelier-validate (root-owned, mode 0644).
# The wrapper script must already exist at /usr/local/bin/run_validate.sh
# (or wherever you prefer — adjust the path below). The image
# `iteralabs/aetelier-validate:v0.1.0` should be present on the host;
# build it once with:
#
#   docker build -t iteralabs/aetelier-validate:v0.1.0 \
#                -f aetelier-sdk/serve/validate.Dockerfile .
#
# A standard /etc/cron.d entry needs an explicit user column.
#
# Cadence rationale: with the default md_worker config (flush_threshold=3600,
# grid=100ms ⇒ ~6-minute parquet files) every 10 minutes lets the validator
# inspect each new file roughly twice without piling up overlapping runs.
# Tighten to */5 if you want quicker feedback or relax to */30 on quiet
# weekends.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MAILTO=ops@example.com

#  ┌─ minute (0-59)
#  │   ┌─ hour (0-23)
#  │   │  ┌─ day of month (1-31)
#  │   │  │ ┌─ month (1-12)
#  │   │  │ │ ┌─ day of week (0-6, Sun=0)
#  │   │  │ │ │ user      command
*/10  *  * * * root      /usr/local/bin/run_validate.sh
